<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karyes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karyes is the administrative centre of the monastic state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Mount Athos</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. It is the seat of the Holy Community, the council of representatives of the twenty ruling monasteries, and of its executive, as well as of a civil governor appointed by the Greek state. Its Protaton church, dating from the 10th century, holds wall paintings by the painter Manuel Panselinos from around 1300.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karyes.jpg" alt="Karyes" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mzgreco7 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Karyes,_Laconia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
